# Data Components API for Custom Item Building

## Overview

The Data Components API allows developers to access and modify item properties beyond what `ItemMeta` provides. According to the documentation, it offers "a version-specific interface for accessing and manipulating item data."

## Key Usage Pattern

The API follows a consistent approach:

```java
// Check for a component
item.hasData(DataComponentTypes.CUSTOM_NAME);

// Read a component
Integer damage = item.getData(DataComponentTypes.DAMAGE);

// Set a component
item.setData(DataComponentTypes.CUSTOM_MODEL_DATA, CustomModelData.customModelData()
    .addFloat(0.5F).build());

// Remove a component
item.unsetData(DataComponentTypes.TOOL);
```

## Building Complex Items

For components with complex structures, builders are required:

```java
ItemStack sword = ItemStack.of(Material.DIAMOND_SWORD);
sword.setData(DataComponentTypes.LORE, ItemLore.lore().addLine(Component.text("Cool!")));
sword.setData(DataComponentTypes.ENCHANTMENTS, ItemEnchantments.itemEnchantments()
    .add(Enchantment.SHARPNESS, 10));
```

## Important Caveats

The API is "designed to adapt to version changes" and "breaking changes made to components by Mojang may result in breaking changes" to this API—backwards compatibility is not guaranteed. Use `ItemMeta` instead if cross-version support is critical.

